# Concurrency Discipline

- Identify shared mutable state, its owner, synchronization primitive, and
  happens-before relation.
- Define lock ordering and never call unknown, blocking, or re-entrant code
  while holding a lock without a proof.
- Bound queues, workers, retries, fan-out, and waiting.
- Make cancellation, timeout, shutdown, and partial startup idempotent.
- Preserve errors from child tasks and join or release every spawned activity.
- Check races, deadlocks, starvation, lost wakeups, duplicate work, stale reads,
  and ordering assumptions.
- Prefer message passing or immutable snapshots when they simplify the proof.
- Add deterministic coordination tests; do not rely on sleeps as correctness.
